        "original_id": "6b083817-59dd-5149-b6d5-eda35e600312",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: KSPN-FM, Talking Heads\n- People: David Byrne, Tom Petty, Van Morrison, Ben Harper, Stephen Thomas Erlewine\n- Music Groups: Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, Widespread Panic\n- Concepts: AAA format, classic rock, new wave music\n- Places: New York City\n- Roles: founding member, principal songwriter, lead singer, guitarist, critic\n\nFacts:\n- David Byrne was born on 14 May 1952 and is a Scottish-born American musician.\n- Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City and active until 1991.\n- David Byrne was the founding member, principal songwriter, lead singer, and guitarist of Talking Heads during the band’s 1975–1991 run.\n- Talking Heads helped pioneer new wave music by combining punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\n- Critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine described Talking Heads as one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the 1980s.\n- KSPN-FM features the AAA format, which mixes classic rock artists such as Tom Petty, Van Morrison, and Talking Heads with newer musicians such as Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, and Widespread Panic.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
